  "verbalization": "Genipin Gentiobioside appears to be a potential target for Jurkat through a series of molecular interactions, with multiple pathways converging on the same target. The evidence suggests that Genipin Gentiobioside acts as a target for HEp-2, which in turn is targeted by Schisandilactone G or Tatridin B, both of which ultimately target Jurkat. This indicates a possible hierarchical relationship where Genipin Gentiobioside may influence HEp-2, which then affects Jurkat through different molecular mechanisms. The presence of multiple distinct targets (Schisandilactone G, Tatridin B, and a complex oxolan compound) suggests that Genipin Gentiobioside may engage in diverse interactions with cellular pathways, potentially modulating Jurkat through varied mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of HEp-2 as a critical mediator in the interaction between Genipin Gentiobioside and Jurkat.",
